      "Payment infrastructure assumes a person authorising a purchase, with the fraud, consent, and dispute mechanisms built around that. An agent buying something on a budget it was given is a different event, and the questions it raises have no established answers. Who authorised it. What limit applied. What happens when the agent was mistaken rather than the merchant fraudulent.",
